# Public kiosk reverse proxy (ADR "Public kiosk demo, Docker Compose on an OpenVZ VM"). Terminates TLS on :443
# with automatic Let's Encrypt certificates for the two public hostnames, redirects :80 → :443, and forwards to
# the app. Caddy adds X-Forwarded-Proto / -Host / -For (the app trusts them via App__TrustProxyHeaders) and
# transparently proxies the SignalR notifications WebSocket.
#
#   demo.simplarchive.dev → the Api (the SPA + API + OIDC + the /hubs SignalR endpoint)
#   s3.simplarchive.dev   → the SeaweedFS S3 API, so the browser can reach presigned upload/download/preview
#                           URLs over HTTPS with no mixed-content. Caddy v2 preserves the incoming Host header,
#                           so SeaweedFS's SigV4 validation matches (the AWS signature covers host, not scheme).
#
# ACME HTTP-01 is served automatically on :80; both A-records must point at this VM before first start.

{
	email admin@simplarchive.dev
}

demo.simplarchive.dev {
	reverse_proxy api:8080
}

s3.simplarchive.dev {
	reverse_proxy seaweedfs:8333
}
